course: dictionary
lesson: 15114
title: Salaried work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some people are paid in a fixed way. A salaried person gets the same fixed amount of money each year, usually split into equal monthly payments. Their pay does not change with the number of hours they work.
explain: «Mum is a salaried teacher, so she gets the same pay every month.» Salaried tells you her pay is fixed. The word comes from salary, the fixed yearly pay that a job gives.
explain: Compare this with hourly pay. «Sam works in a shop and is paid for each hour he works.» Sam is not salaried, because his pay depends on his hours. To check your meaning, swap in "fixed pay every month": if the sentence still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Salaried means paid a fixed amount of money, usually every month.
fact: A salary is the fixed amount of money paid for a job each year.
fact: A salaried job is a job that pays a salary.
fact: To find the monthly pay from a yearly salary, divide by 12. For example, «£24,000 a year» is «£2,000 a month».
fact: Workers who are paid by the hour get money for each hour they work, so their pay can change from month to month.
exercise: «Mum is a salaried teacher.» What does salaried mean here? | Paid in coins only | Not paid at all | Paid for each hour she works | *Paid a fixed amount of money, usually every month
exercise: «Tom is paid for each hour he works at the factory.» Is Tom salaried? | Yes, because factory workers always get a salary | *No, he is paid by the hour, not a fixed salary | Yes, because he has a job
exercise: A salary of £24,000 a year is paid in 12 equal monthly payments. How much is each payment? | £200 | *£2,000 | £12,000 | £20,000
test: «The office manager is salaried, so her pay stays the same every month.» What does this suggest? | Her pay goes up and down with her hours | *Her pay is fixed | She is paid only at Christmas | She works for free
test: A salary of £18,000 a year is paid in 12 equal monthly payments. How much is each payment? | £18,120 | *£1,500 | £15,000 | £180
exam: Which sentence describes a salaried job? | A job where you are paid for every hour you work | A job where you are never paid | A job you do only in the summer | *A job that pays a fixed salary each year
